        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(reporting): harden publication and recovery",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nKova report publication could expose mixed generations, leave partially cleaned report bundles after interruption, and race concurrent writers or retention cleanup. Those failure modes made generated reports and receipts less trustworthy under retries, crashes, or overlapping runs.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis consolidates report publication around one lock contract and one recoverable generation transaction:\n\n- atomic, durable report and receipt publication\n- generation-aware rollback and restart recovery\n- canonical shared file locking with stale-owner recovery and foreign-host safety\n- validated bundle retention that refuses incomplete or mismatched generations\n- explicit incomplete-cleanup reporting\n- release and selfcheck coverage for the complete publication path\n\nThe branch preserves the current `main` auth, artifact, process, release, and collector work while replacing the earlier publication approach with the reviewed recovery model.\n\n## User Impact\n\nReport readers should now see either the previous complete generation or the next complete generation. Interrupted runs recover without deleting unrelated prior files, concurrent writers serialize safely, and retention only removes validated report bundles.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `npm run check:full`\n  - selfcheck: `252/252 PASS`\n  - snapshots: `21/21 PASS`\n  - web payload: `1/1 PASS`\n  - release contract checks passed\n- focused selfchecks:\n  - performance baseline regression\n  - file-lock recovery, including foreign-host ownership\n  - report publication integrity, including torn transaction markers and generation recovery\n  - cleanup publication receipts\n- fresh Sol/high autoreview: clean, no accepted or actionable findings; patch correct at `0.87` confidence\n- branch is rebased onto exact `main` SHA `04c5c8726366c1ff799d77f27ce969b99e6ff46b`\n",
        "branch": "fix/kova-report-publication",
